{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Hear, O YHWH, the voice of Judah.</b> Meaning: because Judah sinned in the matter of Tamar and confessed his sin, saying (Genesis 38:26) ״צָדְקָה מִמֶּנִּי״, Moses asked that YHWH receive his voice in his confession. And he stated this matter to say after it ״וְאֶל עַמּוֹ תְּבִיאֶנּוּ״, meaning according to what we have written on the verse ״מִטֶּרֶף בְּנִי עָלִיתָ״ (Genesis 49:9), for through the act of Tamar he brought forth human prey that the belial had consumed, and this is what he alluded to in saying ״יָדָיו״, meaning the power of his deeds was great for him — he grew great and acquired dominion with an added supernal fence, as we elaborated there." "And His saying <b>and may He be a help from his adversaries.</b> Meaning: although he produced Peretz and Zerach through the act of Tamar, even so the kingdom of the house of David had not yet shone forth, for it needs the holy spark that is still among the nations, namely Ruth the Moabitess. Therefore He said ״וְעֵזֶר מִצָּרָיו תִּהְיֶה״ in the feminine form; moreover, ״עֵזֶר״ points to the female, as it says (Genesis 2:18) ״אֶעֱשֶׂה לּוֹ עֵזֶר״ etc. And see what I have written on the verse ״וְחָטָאתִי לְאָבִי״ etc. (Genesis 43:9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:03.005585220Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}